        "original_id": "0627413f-a08c-5194-a505-5fab62aa9259",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mack V. Wright, Kurt Neumann, Gene Autry, Smiley Burnette, Lois Wilde\n- Roles: actor, film director\n- Places: Nuremberg, Germany, Los Angeles\n- Works: The Singing Cowboy\n- Topics: American film, German Hollywood film, Western films, science fiction movies\n\nFacts:\n- Mack V. Wright was born on 9 March 1894 and died on 14 August 1965.\n- Mack V. Wright was an American actor and film director.\n- The Singing Cowboy is a 1936 American Western film.\n- The Singing Cowboy was directed by Mack V. Wright and starred Gene Autry, Smiley Burnette, and Lois Wilde.\n- Kurt Neumann was born on 5 April 1908 in Nuremberg, Germany.\n- Kurt Neumann was a German Hollywood film director.\n- In his later career, Kurt Neumann specialized in science fiction movies.\n- Kurt Neumann died on 21 August 1958 in Los Angeles.",
